    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "College Success (CS) is a college access program working to increase the number of K-12 students who are prepared to complete a college degree. For my field project, I contributed to a program impact evaluation in collaboration with College Success' Director of Evaluation. Our evaluation sought to assess how effectively College Success meets its goal of increasing college access, fostering college-going culture, and improving college retention among low-income, BIPOC youth. Over the last six months, I helped create evaluation tools, ran a focus group, cleaned, processed, and interpreted quantitative and qualitative data, and developed a data narrative that was shared with CS staff in August. Additionally, I produced a framework for CS staff to draft recommendations, identify program priorities, and develop an implementation timeline informed by our data. My final deliverable, a College Success program impact evaluation report, showcases each step of the evaluation process and our data findings.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Olick, E. (2024). College Success Impact Evaluation. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/ds802wk2338. https://doi.org/10.25740/ds802wk2338.",
